 <figcaption id="schema-control-title"><span class="figure-number">Figure 2</span> A request to stop is an intermediate state</figcaption>
 <div class="schema-scene">
  <p class="schema-kind">Selected documented job paths · not an exhaustive state machine</p>
  <div class="schema-path"><p class="schema-label">Keep the work</p><ol><li>running</li><li>pause-requested</li><li>paused</li></ol><p>RESUME JOB allows work to run again. The candidate remains unfinished while paused.</p></div>
  <div class="schema-path"><p class="schema-label">Abandon a cancellable build</p><ol><li>running</li><li>cancel-requested</li><li>reverting</li><li>canceled</li></ol><p>Reversion withdraws the unfinished schema change. It can itself need retries or fail.</p></div>
  <div class="schema-cleanup"><span>Unusable candidate removed</span><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b><span>Discarded keys may still await garbage collection</span><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b><span>Physical storage is reclaimed later</span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="schema-caption">Requested states and cleanup are separate observations. A job may pass through an intermediate state between polls. A succeeded build needs a new schema change to remove it; cancellation is no longer its undo path.</p>
</figure>
